## Entry 4: Responsive Website Design

**Technique/Framework:** Iterative prompting and device testing

**Purpose:** To make the portfolio accessible on different screen sizes while maintaining the intended desktop design.

**Actual Prompts:**

- "I'm good with the result, my only problem is the responsiveness to different devices, can I deploy it first in github and check it on my phone, if I'm not satisfied can you help me fix it again?"
- "can I try it in my phone?"
- "in desktop it's good you don't have to change anything to that, only in mobile view the logo is centered which it needs to be in left like in my mockup and the title is in right side."

**Result Summary:**

The CSS was adjusted to improve the website's appearance on mobile devices. The Home section was arranged with the logo on the left and the portfolio title centered on the right. The mobile navigation bar was also aligned to the right while remaining sticky.

**Evaluation:**

I tested the website using my mobile phone and requested further adjustments until the layout matched my intended mockup.

